<title>BRAZIL: Brazil reaffirms no shift in forex policy planned.</title>
<headline>Brazil reaffirms no shift in forex policy planned.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian government reaffirmed Wednesday that it was not contemplating any shift in foreign exchange policy.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no change in foreign exchange policy,&quot; said Sergio Amaral, a spokesman for President Fernando Henrique Cardoso.</p>
<p>Brazilian stocks and debt prices plunged Tuesday amid concerns over a possible devaluation of the real, Brazil's currency. The market nervousness vanished Wednesday, and Sao Paulo's Bovespa stock exchange recouped the previous day's losses.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-3141193))</p>
